# INV-05 — invented. Five overs a side: the first side all out for 26 in four.
# Edge cases: ten wickets ending the innings; a wicket on the last ball of an
# over (falls at 0.6) and the new batter at the non-striker's end after the
# change of ends; stumped off a wide (the bowler's wicket, no ball of the
# over: falls at 1.0); a striker run out with no run taken, the batters
# crossed, at the bowler's end; the non-striker run out off a no-ball after a
# run, at the striker's end (falls at 2.0), the free hit that followed hit
# for two and a hit wicket on the ball after it; obstructing the field; a
# four all run (no boundary); a chase won with a six past the target.
